{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro","id":889004,"title":"The broken topic! Power hungry players, let's discuss. (NECRO)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T04:10:38-07:00","id":889004,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The broken topic! Power hungry players, let's discuss. (NECRO)","content":"Hi folks! this is going to be a topic in between both questions and considerations on the spells or combo that u might consider broken/overpowered ... here is my list but i want to hear others opinion as well. Help this poor narrator gamemaster avoid his players from simply bypass everything.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (jk, i am more than used to)<br /> This topic is not (only) purely intended for a min/max lab and powerplayer room but for understanding and bettering the power differences and problems with the setting. <br /> In my mind, i always try to balance things out and if something might be abused i have to find a way to turn it arount the players or build a setting or story that won't permit players to abuse it- NOT frustrating their actions and spells, but rather offering a better chance of challenge and reward after. Like for example, there is a reason why mastigos or mages with space simply don't go around casting hexes to anyone and mind controling an entire city (i'm exaggerating of course), and that's probabl because every mage learn at least 1 dot of space or is well aware of the danger of that arcana.- Why the idea of mind controling a werewolf or a vampire from ur sanctum isn't a good one? paradox risk, finding the right connection or simpathy, haveing to deal with an ENTIRE pack or coterie and all their allies (spirits with unusual powes that can contest the mind control) ecc...<br /> <br /> 1) time 2- veil of moments- i'm not sure if i understand this spells correctly, but it seems to shield the mage from basically everything, from poison to conditions to physical trauma. So if i stab the mage that has this spell on... do i kill him or not? does the knife slice through his flesh and &quot;ruins&quot; it or does the time stop permit the mage to basically be immune to ANYTHING that time might stop . I discussed it with my players, and we come to the conclusion that the mage does still sufers damage from direct attacks, but he doesn't worsen with time so for example if he gets sliced on his wrists he won't lose 1 healt dot per turn or if he is set on fire, he won't suffer damage on consqeuient turns... but he DOES get hit or stabbed or shot ecc... so the damage resister on his health bar.<br /> If on the other hand im wrong-- either i will house rule this spell or make it that for the duration the mage doesn't suffer any damage, but at the end of the spell every conditon or healt level he would have suffered is inflicted at once on him.<br /> <br /> 2) the acanthus defense- i'm untouchable !!&quot; seriosuly, if an acanthus really wants he can become impossible to hit or almost, at least according to the rules. Since fate armor attainmen adds fate to his defense, and time acceleration adds potency to his defense when dodging, this means that if an acanthus has both effects on has a huge amount of dice for dodging and probably won't suffer a scratch for as long as he is dodging. Did i calculate it right? For exmpale, if an acanthus with fate 3 and time 3 has acceleration and doges, assuming his base defense is just 4 he would dodge at 20 dices ? Do i add all the fate and time dots to defense?<br /> let's do the math defense 2+ fate armor 3+ time acceleration effect 3= 10 defense, when dodging 20. 0_0<br /> according to the rules.. yep.<br /> i would rule this spell as &quot;vulgar&quot; and a breaking point and quiescence for humans in the area, if they see something like a guy dodging like a celerity vampire elder.<br /> Luckily, a simple mage with prime dispellation.. and your dodging ability simply disappear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3) In general, space. Space is one of the most powerful arcana in the book. Not only it allows u to scry or block the passage/attacks of enemies alltogether or seal a person in a dimensional pocket impossible to escape (all with space 3), but the simpathy casting--- isnt't it a little too easy to actually pull off when u have the components? Like, seriously tell me if i get it right. Let's assume i have some kind of connection with a vampire or another supernatural being.. i cast on him a hex or something else and all i have to do is whitstand simpathy+1/ Or his resolve/whatever attribute +1? According to the rules, when u whitsand for multiple factors (Like simpathy casting for example) u simply add +1 for each additional whitstanding to the HIGHER whitstand rating. So if my connection is a strong one like an object or a body sample, i could always find and cast on a poor guy /vampire/promethean ecc... all for his whitstand attribute+1? Am i right or wrong here? tell me please ...<br /> also... seriosuly to target a guy i only require to have met him maybe a couple of times and build a representational tool? Like a doll? Or do i also need body sample or personal belongings to target him.<br /> <br /> How i solve it in my head- space is simply broken and essential for all mages. Even newbies and non combatant learn at least 1 dot of space<br /> Vs other supernaturals- since usually the mage is going to cast with a ritual casting on simpathy, most supernaturals will have time to react/move their allies/influences- ask for help. A vampire can mobilize humans or call for help his allies, a werewolf might step in the umbra (and thus it would be impossible for the mage to reach him unless he has spirit right?)... etc.. ecc..<br /> also i would house rule that if the subject of the spell is in a crowded area where humans gather and the magic is too &quot;flashy&quot; the effect would be paradoxical and the abyss would reach to hit the arrogant mage... what do u think?<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) turn momentum, forces 3... simply allow mages to dodge anything? Since everything in physics and reality needs momentum to hit a target... <br /> <br /> How do i solve it in my head- either the mage needs to see the targets before he cast the spells (so in 1 turn he has to activate and decide which objects he will deflect) or he also has to apply scale and size factors for it to be effective. Like dodging a car or a werewolf would require adcanced scale. What do u think? And of course, if a mage use this in a place full of humans shooting at him POINT BLANK and not hitting him... it should call for a paradox roll.<br /> <br /> 4) Does the spell 2 death.. suppress life.. suppress life??<br /> like i can simply cast it on a dude and he will faint and collapse like a dead corpse for the duration.. that seems broken to me or at least it should call for a whitstand... or maybe i'm just not understanding the spell at all and the subject &quot;appears&quot; like a zombie but still walks and act normally, his heart doesn't beat and the body temperatures drop.<br /> Same with ghost gate. It seems to imply that a mage simply touch a person and can teleport him in Twilight without even whitstand the effect (?)<br /> <br /> 5) Hung spells-- with fate added. Anyone here who is or was a dungeons master knows the danger and power of spells like contingency... but how many spells exactly can i hang? The spell says spells equal to potency so a potency 3 hang could suspend maximum 3 spells at once? Do i have to cast them all at once?<br /> And most important.. the factors of the hanged spells can be modified right? I can apply reach, factors and penalities so that when the spell is relead it will have advanced potency, duration ecc... am i right?<br /> <br /> Luckily hung spells are easily to become double edged knives.. if the player doesn't specify well planned conditions he will suffer from hang spells released at inappropriate times or nor released at all. (example &quot;it will activate when i get attacked!&quot; but if someone ambush the mage and he doesn't realize it, he will get hit normally, or if he gets simply dominated or charmed).<br /> also.. do hang spells activate in the same turn if multiple, and does it take an action to have them? Or its simply a reflexive thing and they pop up when the condition sets in?<br /> <br /> 6) Prime. I LOVE prime. seriosuly. It's one of my favourite arcana. It solve magically all of the above problems with the swing of a wand. Did u hang spells, prepare ur force field, cast ur magic armor on u ecc. ecc.??... well son i have bad news for u..<br /> <br /> what do u think? what are ur personal broken combo/ overpowered stats or spells that u house rule or simply have to deal with?<br /> <br /> I like a world where things even if unfair, get balanced (or not, like real world). For exmple, vampires might not be able to curse u while they sit in their havens, but they can easily ruin ur life and moving entire &quot;armies&quot; of contacts, allies, ghouls.. ecc.. and if they really wanted to give a mage an hard time.. they could just use humans! Humans are just the worst for a mage, especially if in a crowd. While u have to think twice before call a lighting or curse the leech, he can simply catch u in a street with tons of people and rip ur earth out while obfuscated (ecc..ecc.. the possibilities are endless).<br /> werewolves have packs, gifts and fucking spirits. Powerful spirits like totems can contest the arcana and get angry if they find out someone is messing with their guardians. not even talking about the actual act of kiling a werewolf since they regenerate everything and can rage in hulk mode ignoring mind control too (almost).<br /> <br /> What do u guys think? Show us the horrors of ur goup/players! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T06:55:23-07:00","id":889072,"title":"","content":"Pun-Pun like Mastigos trick:<br /> Klara the Mastigos likes Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill, and Enhance Attribute. She likes them so much that she picks them as her Rotes, which key off her favorite Skill.<br /> Klara casts Enhance Skill using her Rote, targeting her Favorite Skill. She pays Mana and Reach to push it over Human limits. Her Favorite Skill is higher, so her Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill and Enhance Attribute dicepools are now bigger. Which means that she can cast Enhance Skill again, with more Potency! This means that her Skill will become bigger, by a point or two than in previous casting, allowing her to repeat this until she arrives at Infinity.<br /> After gaining Infinite Skill, Klara decides to become Infinitely Smart. She casts Enhance Attribute, using her Infinite Dicepool to set her Traits at Infinity. After becoming Infinitely Smart, she understands now what should be done to humanity.<br /> She casts Psychic Domination, with Duration set to Indefinite, and pays Reach to get most powerful command ever imagined. She puts Infinite Factors into everything, so whole Universe is covered by her spell, which has only one command:<br /> WATCH. CAT. VIDEOS.<br /> And then, Klara the Mastigos ascends, becoming Dark Mittens Mittens, Exarch of Control Through Kittens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-12-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T06:56:38-07:00","id":889074,"title":"","content":"Long post dude <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, lets begin with <b>Veil of Moments (Time 2)</b>. Read carefully and you will see that you only are inmune to things that worse with time, like bleeding, sickness, poisons and so. You can't get new <i>conditions</i> or <i>tilts</i> (good or bad), but if it's a supernatural condition there is a clash of wills.<br /> So if someone shoots you, you are hurt. If someone uses a Terrorize (Mind 4) spell on you, there is a clash of wills. And your previous conditions don't worsen, but they are still working on you. <b>Temporal Summoning (Time 3)</b> is needed to suspend conditions and wounds for a time.<br /> <br /> More subjects later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:20:58-07:00","id":889091,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of infinite mana combos that I've heard of so far. One is to just cast Shifting Sands after you've taken the mana from somewhere. The other is to alternate casting Devouring the Slain and Quicken Ghost on a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:24:29-07:00","id":889095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro#post889004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) turn momentum, forces 3... simply allow mages to dodge anything? Since everything in physics and reality needs momentum to hit a target...<br /> <br /> How do i solve it in my head- either the mage needs to see the targets before he cast the spells (so in 1 turn he has to activate and decide which objects he will deflect) or he also has to apply scale and size factors for it to be effective. Like dodging a car or a werewolf would require adcanced scale. What do u think? And of course, if a mage use this in a place full of humans shooting at him POINT BLANK and not hitting him... it should call for a paradox roll.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe we getting getting a bit over excited. Like most times we believe something is super powerful until we understand its limitations.<br /> <br /> (page145)<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can use Turn Momentum\u2019s effect as a<br /> reflexive action instead.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage may control where the object is redirected<br /> to, as long as it is within 90 degrees of the original arc<br /> in any direction.<br /> +2 Reach: The object\u2019s momentum can be fully reversed.<br /> Thrown and Ranged weapons strike their users.<br /> Add Time \u2022: With Time 1 and a Reach, the mage can turn objects too fast for her to gain Defense against them.<br /> <br /> Spell potency allows you a number of times/targets you can use this ablity, so about three. Then you add in spell factors like time and scale to effect larger stuff and have a more open window to use the number of charges. and then reach list implyes that the use of this free dodge is a use of your turn/standard action, and to use it as a reflex you must spend reach.<br /> <br /> as far point blank<br /> language::<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ae6B7C05Nk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ae6B7C05Nk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ae6B7C05Nk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ae6B7C05Nk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:47:40-07:00","id":889111,"title":"","content":"Present as Past - you automatically win initiative against everyone but other Time mages. With Temporal Sympathy, you can use Temporal Summons to turn your enemy back into a completely human child, or a Rank 0 mote, anything. As long as you can beat a Clash of Wills and get enough dice, Temporal Summons can defeat anything by rendering it into a powerless form unable to fight back. <br /> <br /> When taken together, Time Mastery means that you always go first, you're never surprised, and when you do act, you win. If you're Acanthus, then expect to get lots of Fate boosts to make sure you never fail the rolls either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:00:25-07:00","id":889119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889111#post889111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Present as Past - you automatically win initiative against everyone but other Time mages. With Temporal Sympathy, you can use Temporal Summons to turn your enemy back into a completely human child, or a Rank 0 mote, anything. As long as you can beat a Clash of Wills and get enough dice, Temporal Summons can defeat anything by rendering it into a powerless form unable to fight back.<br /> <br /> When taken together, Time Mastery means that you always go first, you're never surprised, and when you do act, you win. If you're Acanthus, then expect to get lots of Fate boosts to make sure you never fail the rolls either.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah this one felt really weird to me. Present as past. why add the line about other supers? it feels odd because this is the same things that celerity does. why not let them clash of wills as well and enjoy the counter play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:08:26-07:00","id":889125,"title":"","content":"Temporal Summoning feels like a 5 dot spell. It even recreates a whole Death 5 Spell (deny the Reaper), down to the point of ressurecting dead. Temporal Sympathy isn't a big deal, because it has Withstand of 3 at best (so not much), and you can get a symbolical representation of subject by making a stick baby drawing with &quot;&lt;-- BABY YOU&quot; written next to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-12-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:09:25-07:00","id":889127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889072#post889072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pun-Pun like Mastigos trick:<br /> Klara the Mastigos likes Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill, and Enhance Attribute. She likes them so much that she picks them as her Rotes, which key off her favorite Skill.<br /> Klara casts Enhance Skill using her Rote, targeting her Favorite Skill. She pays Mana and Reach to push it over Human limits. Her Favorite Skill is higher, so her Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill and Enhance Attribute dicepools are now bigger. Which means that she can cast Enhance Skill again, with more Potency! This means that her Skill will become bigger, by a point or two than in previous casting, allowing her to repeat this until she arrives at Infinity.<br /> After gaining Infinite Skill, Klara decides to become Infinitely Smart. She casts Enhance Attribute, using her Infinite Dicepool to set her Traits at Infinity. After becoming Infinitely Smart, she understands now what should be done to humanity.<br /> She casts Psychic Domination, with Duration set to Indefinite, and pays Reach to get most powerful command ever imagined. She puts Infinite Factors into everything, so whole Universe is covered by her spell, which has only one command:<br /> WATCH. CAT. VIDEOS.<br /> And then, Klara the Mastigos ascends, becoming Dark Mittens Mittens, Exarch of Control Through Kittens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zvEWFjWfqiU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zvEWFjWfqiU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zvEWFjWfqiU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/zvEWFjWfqiU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1321-bael-the-cruel","name":"Bael the Cruel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1321_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:25:10-07:00","id":889132,"title":"","content":"While I find the idea of infinity skill amusing it is incorrect in practice.<br /> <br /> page 160-161<br /> + 2 Reach: By spending a point of Mana, the mage may increase<br /> her subject\u2019s Skills above the normal maximum allowed.<br /> <br /> not to mention that each casting of the spell counts towards spell control, so plus one reach beyond your gnosis slot for each casting. +3reach, +4reach, +5reach ect. Unless you want to lose that control, which is a bad idea and invites trouble. Probability says you'll explode paradox before you'll reach 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:30:30-07:00","id":889138,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the rule against spell stacking shut that down right quick?<br /> <br /> Personally, my favorite trick as an Acanthus is to swear an Oath to do something I plan on doing anyway, letting me gain free perks for following through on whatever plan I like. Bonus points if you give yourself an easy escape condition just in case.<br /> <br /> &quot;I swear that unless I snap my fingers three times while hopping on one leg, I will l hunt down the mage who killed my master and take my revenge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then when it turns out your master faked his death to motivate you for some trial, you can just let yourself out of the oath without killing him for no consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 05-12-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:33:18-07:00","id":889140,"title":"","content":"Time... I think that Time, given how little love it had in the past, was given a lot of new stuff that it didn't have before, but inadvertantly was made too strong. Time can resurrect the dead, remove supernatural templates, and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:38:10-07:00","id":889146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889140#post889140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time... I think that Time, given how little love it had in the past, was given a lot of new stuff that it didn't have before, but inadvertantly was made too strong. Time can resurrect the dead, remove supernatural templates, and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporarily (haha get it?). I don't think any of that stuff is permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:43:25-07:00","id":889151,"title":"","content":"Yes and no. Like all spells, any of it can be made Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:45:56-07:00","id":889152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889111#post889111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Present as Past - you automatically win initiative against everyone but other Time mages. With Temporal Sympathy, you can use Temporal Summons to turn your enemy back into a completely human child, or a Rank 0 mote, anything. As long as you can beat a Clash of Wills and get enough dice, Temporal Summons can defeat anything by rendering it into a powerless form unable to fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, that strategy didn't work out too well for Ura Urashima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:49:35-07:00","id":889155,"title":"","content":"Hm another Time trick: The Hung Spell Doom Loop.<br /> <br /> Cast Hung Spell with at least three slots for spells to hang.<br /> Cast any spells in to Hung Spell, but save the last for another Hung spell.<br /> Cast Hung Spell in to the last slot.<br /> Repeat steps 1-3 until you have as many spells hung as you feel you need.<br /> With Fate 2, set a condition to end the first Hung Spell.<br /> When the condition is met, watch someone get hit with dozens of spells at once.<br /> <br /> Granted, it only works once, and only on a single target, but goddamn that person is going to have a bad day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 05-12-2016, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:51:51-07:00","id":889158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889151#post889151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. Like all spells, any of it can be made Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope: all spell can be cast as indefinite, but only a small part as lasting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:02:29-07:00","id":889165,"title":"","content":"ok going back to enhance spell for a second look.<br /> <br /> implying top states 10gnosis 5arcane 5yanmax = 20pool. page112(you apply penalties then add yanthmax)<br /> <br /> you get 5 pot for free from arcane. You can go -5in dice pool before its simply impossible to even attempt. Each potecny costs 2 dice. so you 10(20dice)+2(4dice) = 12 pot AND if you assume max stat(at gnosis10 its 10) = 22 on a chance die for one turn. good job sir, you are beyond our mortal comprehension x4++ master at your craft. but no where near infinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:03:55-07:00","id":889166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889138#post889138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the rule against spell stacking shut that down right quick?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it wont help. Spell stacking rules prohibit you from something like this:<br /> &quot;I cast Enhance Skill with Potency 3, Raising it by 3, and then I cast Potency 3 Enhance Skill again, for +6!&quot;<br /> Stacking rules will tell you that only highest Potency version of this spell will work, with rest laying dormant. However, what Dark Mittens Mittens did, is like this:<br /> 1. Casting Enhance Skill with Potency Y boosts her dicepool on Enhance Skill.<br /> 2. This means she can cast Enhance Skill with Potency Y+Z. <br /> 3. Because Potency Y+Z is bigger than Potency Y, Spell Stacking rules say that your new spell overtakes the previous one. Basically, your Skill rises up by the difference between PotencyY+Z - PotencyY (so by Z). <br /> 4. Basically, you climb the mountain; first casting allows you for more powerful second casting, which allows you more powerful third casting, and so on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:05:38-07:00","id":889168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889091#post889091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple of infinite mana combos that I've heard of so far. One is to just cast Shifting Sands after you've taken the mana from somewhere. The other is to alternate casting Devouring the Slain and Quicken Ghost on a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can also grab a familiar and use Essence Fountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:23:55-07:00","id":889180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889165#post889165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok going back to enhance spell for a second look.<br /> <br /> implying top states 10gnosis 5arcane 5yanmax = 20pool. page112(you apply penalties then add yanthmax)<br /> <br /> you get 5 pot for free from arcane. You can go -5in dice pool before its simply impossible to even attempt. Each potecny costs 2 dice. so you 10(20dice)+2(4dice) = 12 pot AND if you assume max stat(at gnosis10 its 10) = 22 on a chance die for one turn. good job sir, you are beyond our mortal comprehension x4++ master at your craft. but no where near infinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 is not maximum Yantra. 5 is maximum leftover yantras not spent on Spell Factors. However, you are right, you can't go under -5 even with Yantra bonuses. A good failsafe! Still, you can make it pretty big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:49:33-07:00","id":889204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889180#post889180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 is not maximum Yantra. 5 is maximum leftover yantras not spent on Spell Factors. However, you are right, you can't go under -5 even with Yantra bonuses. A good failsafe! Still, you can make it pretty big.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed mate. one of the things I like chronicals over world is that you can understand the scaling a lot better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:06:26-07:00","id":889216,"title":"","content":"I totally forgot about the -5 rule. I remember that I really got excited about it, too, because it puts a restriction on Master Ritual Bullshit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:41:45-07:00","id":889232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889132#post889132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I find the idea of infinity skill amusing it is incorrect in practice.<br /> <br /> page 160-161<br /> + 2 Reach: By spending a point of Mana, the mage may increase<br /> her subject\u2019s Skills above the normal maximum allowed.<br /> <br /> not to mention that each casting of the spell counts towards spell control, so plus one reach beyond your gnosis slot for each casting. +3reach, +4reach, +5reach ect. Unless you want to lose that control, which is a bad idea and invites trouble. Probability says you'll explode paradox before you'll reach 20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a good limitation, assuming that you have to follow it at the time of the casting. As I recall, the infinity skill trick (and a great many things) start off by taking the four dot sanctum merit to have a demesne in your sanctum. This prevents you from suffering paradox as long as you do not meet a sleeper within the duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> So; Assuming you have a rote for enhance skill (or gain skill, but if you have gain skill your even better equipped than the following example) and you have Mind 3, Gnosis 3, and Skill rank 3. I would in this scenario:<br /> <br /> Apply Reach to duration so that the spell doesn't last a few seconds<br /> Apply Reach to the skill limitation so that it can raise above 3<br /> Apply Reach to the Primary Factor to change it from 'duration' to 'potency', because I don't need a long lasting ritual yet.<br /> Then I would apply a -4 penalty and roll Mind 3 + Gnosis 3 + Verge 2 + Skill Mudra 3 = 8 Dice, For 8 Dice to cast a potency 5 spell.<br /> <br /> I would then immediately repeat this, except the next time I would take a -8 penalty, because my skill would be 8 then, to create an 8 potency spell. So on, so forth. Release and cast until you reach the point where your potency is happily high enough to apply to all traits. By the time you leave your sanctum, at which point you will make the final spell indefinate. the only spell about to incur paradox is the indefinate one in the end, because you will have been in a verge for the duration of the rest.<br /> <br /> ... I suppose I could keep the Primary Factor as Duration, and spend a reach to make it Instant cast instead (and that duration would then give you enough time to cast your next spell).<br /> <br /> I think the real limitation to that is more the fact that you'd run out of mana and have to restock and start again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Just realized that rotes get free Reach as though the caster had 5 dots in the Arcana. So with a Mind 3 effect, you'd have 3 free reach. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-12-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:02:22-07:00","id":889379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889095#post889095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do believe we getting getting a bit over excited. Like most times we believe something is super powerful until we understand its limitations.<br /> <br /> (page145)<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can use Turn Momentum\u2019s effect as a<br /> reflexive action instead.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage may control where the object is redirected<br /> to, as long as it is within 90 degrees of the original arc<br /> in any direction.<br /> +2 Reach: The object\u2019s momentum can be fully reversed.<br /> Thrown and Ranged weapons strike their users.<br /> Add Time \u2022: With Time 1 and a Reach, the mage can turn objects too fast for her to gain Defense against them.<br /> <br /> Spell potency allows you a number of times/targets you can use this ablity, so about three. Then you add in spell factors like time and scale to effect larger stuff and have a more open window to use the number of charges. and then reach list implyes that the use of this free dodge is a use of your turn/standard action, and to use it as a reflex you must spend reach.<br /> <br /> as far point blank<br /> language::<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ae6B7C05Nk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ae6B7C05Nk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That last reference killed me XD thanks for ur input man","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:06:48-07:00","id":889383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889074#post889074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long post dude <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, lets begin with <b>Veil of Moments (Time 2)</b>. Read carefully and you will see that you only are inmune to things that worse with time, like bleeding, sickness, poisons and so. You can't get new <i>conditions</i> or <i>tilts</i> (good or bad), but if it's a supernatural condition there is a clash of wills.<br /> So if someone shoots you, you are hurt. If someone uses a Terrorize (Mind 4) spell on you, there is a clash of wills. And your previous conditions don't worsen, but they are still working on you. <b>Temporal Summoning (Time 3)</b> is needed to suspend conditions and wounds for a time.<br /> <br /> More subjects later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank u for ur answer man I appreciate it. As I suspected. BuT I don't fully understand how time summoning could actually make me immune to further damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:17:50-07:00","id":889391,"title":"","content":"Not too broken, per se, but &quot;Control Weather&quot; to create a storm beforehand, + &quot;Call lightning&quot;. The funny thing is &quot;you use the rules for electricity&quot;. Lightning -&gt; 10B. You can improve the scale to deal 10B to all targets. If you find a way to be protected from the rest of people, you can spam the same thing on your enemy until it goes to full aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:43:30-07:00","id":889401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889391#post889391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not too broken, per se, but &quot;Control Weather&quot; to create a storm beforehand, + &quot;Call lightning&quot;. The funny thing is &quot;you use the rules for electricity&quot;. Lightning -&gt; 10B. You can improve the scale to deal 10B to all targets. If you find a way to be protected from the rest of people, you can spam the same thing on your enemy until it goes to full aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is called Shielding: Lightning, using Alchemist Touch as the Basis but with Forces. <br /> <br /> Use the appropriate reach to be immune to all damage from it, then giggle as you rain the holy, cleansing wrath of an angry Zeus upon the world around you and walk away unscathed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:59:06-07:00","id":889411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889391#post889391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not too broken, per se, but &quot;Control Weather&quot; to create a storm beforehand, + &quot;Call lightning&quot;. The funny thing is &quot;you use the rules for electricity&quot;. Lightning -&gt; 10B. You can improve the scale to deal 10B to all targets. If you find a way to be protected from the rest of people, you can spam the same thing on your enemy until it goes to full aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> i was thinking the same while reading that spell. Wrath of Thor/Zeus on earth. add reach and u can fry like 5 people in 1 turn... wow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:04:29-07:00","id":889416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889140#post889140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time... I think that Time, given how little love it had in the past, was given a lot of new stuff that it didn't have before, but inadvertantly was made too strong. Time can resurrect the dead, remove supernatural templates, and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it that powerful? i mean, i read the spell description and i don't think i fully comprehend it. Like, if i find myself in front of my enemy, and i have the correct temporal simpathy (for example a pic of him during his childhood) given the right reaches and penalities.. i can just win the whitstand and turn him into a 6 years old??? like.. what the heck. all for a whitstand of 3 and a clash of wills??<br /> I would argue that its only temporary though, and when the spell finish even if i kill him my enemy won't stay dead for very long, since he will return as his old self (comes back from the dead and is still fresh as when i morphed him.) What do u think? Since the spell clearly says the change is temporary and it can even bring back the dead to life.... that would mean that when the spell is finished he will simply &quot;restore&quot; back to his previous condition, ergo still alive.<br /> Anyway, i agree on time it was really improved.<br /> <br /> Edit- nevermind i was stupid... i didn't read the full description of the spell. ok, that's a kind of magic that either i'm going to house rule or change and add whitstand cause its absolutely broken in my opinion....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":".  i was stupid.. 05-12-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum