of effect spells the mage may cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The forces 4 attainment only prevents against undirected elements, not aimed spells. I am sure that includes those you aim at yourself. <br /> <br /> But yeah, adding fate makes things work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:21:48-07:00","id":889429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889423#post889423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forces 4 attainment only prevents against undirected elements, not aimed spells. I am sure that includes those you aim at yourself.<br /> <br /> But yeah, adding fate makes things work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, I guess the casting mage could counterspell his own effect with Forces or Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:44:08-07:00","id":889457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889401#post889401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is called Shielding: Lightning, using Alchemist Touch as the Basis but with Forces.<br /> <br /> Use the appropriate reach to be immune to all damage from it, then giggle as you rain the holy, cleansing wrath of an angry Zeus upon the world around you and walk away unscathed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see that. Though I was reffering more to &quot;Oh, you did that? Guess who'll be my next target... <b><i>*aims at the mage*</i></b> &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:58:36-07:00","id":889468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889429#post889429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, I guess the casting mage could counterspell his own effect with Forces or Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure counterspell disrupts the whole casting, so counterspelling your own spell would mean no lightning for anyone... Though I could have missed something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889457#post889457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I can see that. Though I was reffering more to &quot;Oh, you did that? Guess who'll be my next target... <b><i>*aims at the mage*</i></b> &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering most people would be trying to stay conscious (stamina 5 and size 5 means 1 bolt of lightning fills your hit boxes if no magical armor blocks it), I don't know how good their aim will be (with a -3 penalty, even if they roll to stay conscious)<br /> <br /> Then again, I could just be throwing these boots while sitting on my toilet looking at your most recent Facebook photo as my sympathetic yantra...Talk about Zeus on his Throne <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:22:57-07:00","id":889488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889416#post889416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it that powerful? i mean, i read the spell description and i don't think i fully comprehend it. Like, if i find myself in front of my enemy, and i have the correct temporal simpathy (for example a pic of him during his childhood) given the right reaches and penalities.. i can just win the whitstand and turn him into a 6 years old??? like.. what the heck. all for a whitstand of 3 and a clash of wills??<br /> I would argue that its only temporary though, and when the spell finish even if i kill him my enemy won't stay dead for very long, since he will return as his old self (comes back from the dead and is still fresh as when i morphed him.) What do u think? Since the spell clearly says the change is temporary and it can even bring back the dead to life.... that would mean that when the spell is finished he will simply &amp;quot;restore&amp;quot; back to his previous condition, ergo still alive.<br /> Anyway, i agree on time it was really improved.<br /> <br /> Edit- nevermind i was stupid... i didn't read the full description of the spell. ok, that's a kind of magic that either i'm going to house rule or change and add whitstand cause its absolutely broken in my opinion....</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lack of Withstood might be an error, based on the guidelines and other spells with related effects. I'll treat it as such in any game I run, if it isn't errata'd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:43:17-07:00","id":889502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889416#post889416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it that powerful? i mean, i read the spell description and i don't think i fully comprehend it. Like, if i find myself in front of my enemy, and i have the correct temporal simpathy (for example a pic of him during his childhood) given the right reaches and penalities.. i can just win the whitstand and turn him into a 6 years old??? like.. what the heck. all for a whitstand of 3 and a clash of wills??</div> </div> </div> </div>It lasts a single turn unless you take penalties or spend a Reach to make the Duration Advanced or the primary spell factor, it's Withstood by at least two different things if you're using any Temporal Sympathy worse than Unchanged (which already means you need to tack one onto whichever the worse rating was that you needed to beat, plus another one if you don't know the right name), it takes <i>two Reach</i> to affect a supernatural creature with it <i>at all</i>, you have to spend the Reach for sensory range to use the necessary Attainment, and of course doing any of this on an immediate scale like you'll probably want to do if you &quot;find yourself in front of&quot; your target takes another Reach.<br /> <br /> Rewrite History is an Adept-level spell. You have two free Reach on it at most.<br /> <br /> Undoing a supernatural template for a scene as an instant action at Mastery requires\u2026<br /> <br /> 2 Reach to affect a supernatural target.<br /> 1 Reach to use instant casting (which you can convert to 1 Mana with Time in a Bottle).<br /> 1 Reach to use sensory range (as required for Temporal Sympathy).<br /> 1 Reach to use the Advanced Duration table.<br /> <br /> You need Gnosis 5 at minimum for Mastery of a single Arcanum and this setup already puts you at two Reach over your safe budget, which means six Paradox dice \u2014 four if you've got an appropriate Dedicated Tool on hand (the use of which already makes the casting take multiple turns thanks to the required Yantra for Temporal Sympathy), and as little as zero if you're willing to spend multiple turns and blow two thirds of your maximum available Mana on mitigating Paradox after the Attainments' surcharges.<br /> <br /> You also have to contend with a Withstand rating of at least 4, assuming you know the target's sympathetic name and they don't have a Resolve rating higher than 3 (and if either or both of those things are not the case then you either wasted a spell or need to pump the Potency up with penalties that may not be offset by any extra Yantras you used).<br /> <br /> Depending on your Wisdom, you may have to eat a breaking point roll for releasing any resulting Paradox (which itself can cut the Duration back down to a single turn with one success) or else deal with the complications that containing the Paradox entails.<br /> <br /> You can lessen some of these problems by having a rote of the spell and Gnosis 4/Time 4, but this further contrivance tends to harm this kind of argument. &quot;Absolutely broken&quot; it ain't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Neglected the other Time Attainment. 05-12-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T18:14:32-07:00","id":889517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889502#post889502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rewrite History is an Adept-level spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the spell being discussed is Temporal Summoning, which is a way more powerful debuff, at a 3-dot rating, and which doesn't currently list any Withstood option in the description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T18:39:58-07:00","id":889530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eggs Maledict</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889517#post889517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the spell being discussed is Temporal Summoning, which is a way more powerful debuff, at a 3-dot rating, and which doesn't currently list any Withstood option in the description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal withstand page 186","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T19:00:47-07:00","id":889543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889072#post889072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pun-Pun like Mastigos trick:<br /> Klara the Mastigos likes Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill, and Enhance Attribute. She likes them so much that she picks them as her Rotes, which key off her favorite Skill.<br /> Klara casts Enhance Skill using her Rote, targeting her Favorite Skill. She pays Mana and Reach to push it over Human limits. Her Favorite Skill is higher, so her Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill and Enhance Attribute dicepools are now bigger. Which means that she can cast Enhance Skill again, with more Potency! This means that her Skill will become bigger, by a point or two than in previous casting, allowing her to repeat this until she arrives at Infinity.<br /> After gaining Infinite Skill, Klara decides to become Infinitely Smart. She casts Enhance Attribute, using her Infinite Dicepool to set her Traits at Infinity. After becoming Infinitely Smart, she understands now what should be done to humanity..</div> </div> </div> </div>How did she get infinity mana, and how did she get the time to cast Enhance Skill infinity times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T19:31:41-07:00","id":889574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889530#post889530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporal withstand page 186</div> </div> </div> </div>Spell can be used without Temporal Sympathy on Unchanged-level past versions of the subject without another listed Withstand rating, which, yeah, seems more like an error than an actual problem with the spell itself given that a higher-level spell capable of a similar feat is Withstood and doesn't have quite the baseline potential to outright reduce the target's Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:24:42-07:00","id":889627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889530#post889530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporal withstand page 186</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's a pretty low bar given that it's Potency Primary, on a 3-dot effect, with a maximum Temporal Withstand rating of 3. It should be Withstood: Resolve along with the Temporal Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:55:44-07:00","id":889648,"title":"","content":"Another Acanthus trick:<br /> <br /> Lucky Mana Reactor: At chargen, set your Gnosis at 3 by spending all your bonus points on it. Then set your highest Arcanum to Fate 3 and pick Exceptional Luck as a Praxes. Gnosis 3 + Fate 3 = 6 dice, or, on average 3 successes. Since it's a Praxes, you'll be considered rolling an exceptional success on your spell casting roll with three successes. One of the options on a exceptional success is to not only regain all mana spent, but to gain one additional point of mana. Considering it's omni-applicability you'll be casting it a lot, and with that extra Reach you'll be casting it quickly. This means on average you'll be generating more mana than you put in to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 05-13-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:57:37-07:00","id":889676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889502#post889502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lasts a single turn unless you take penalties or spend a Reach to make the Duration Advanced or the primary spell factor, it's Withstood by at least two different things if you're using any Temporal Sympathy worse than Unchanged (which already means you need to tack one onto whichever the worse rating was that you needed to beat, plus another one if you don't know the right name), it takes <i>two Reach</i> to affect a supernatural creature with it <i>at all</i>, you have to spend the Reach for sensory range to use the necessary Attainment, and of course doing any of this on an immediate scale like you'll probably want to do if you &amp;quot;find yourself in front of&amp;quot; your target takes another Reach.<br /> <br /> Rewrite History is an Adept-level spell. You have two free Reach on it at most.<br /> <br /> Undoing a supernatural template for a scene as an instant action at Mastery requires\u2026<br /> <br /> 2 Reach to affect a supernatural target.<br /> 1 Reach to use instant casting (which you can convert to 1 Mana with Time in a Bottle).<br /> 1 Reach to use sensory range (as required for Temporal Sympathy).<br /> 1 Reach to use the Advanced Duration table.<br /> <br /> You need Gnosis 5 at minimum for Mastery of a single Arcanum and this setup already puts you at two Reach over your safe budget, which means six Paradox dice \u2014 four if you've got an appropriate Dedicated Tool on hand (the use of which already makes the casting take multiple turns thanks to the required Yantra for Temporal Sympathy), and as little as zero if you're willing to spend multiple turns and blow two thirds of your maximum available Mana on mitigating Paradox after the Attainments' surcharges.<br /> <br /> You also have to contend with a Withstand rating of at least 4, assuming you know the target's sympathetic name and they don't have a Resolve rating higher than 3 (and if either or both of those things are not the case then you either wasted a spell or need to pump the Potency up with penalties that may not be offset by any extra Yantras you used).<br /> <br /> Depending on your Wisdom, you may have to eat a breaking point roll for releasing any resulting Paradox (which itself can cut the Duration back down to a single turn with one success) or else deal with the complications that containing the Paradox entails.<br /> <br /> You can lessen some of these problems by having a rote of the spell and Gnosis 4/Time 4, but this further contrivance tends to harm this kind of argument. &amp;quot;Absolutely broken&amp;quot; it ain't.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be totally fine with me and I absolutely agree with u except that the spell we are discussing is temporale summoning (time 3) which a part from temporal simpathy list no Whitstand at all aND quotes &quot;a mage can restore ancient ruines, or turn his enemies into babies.&quot; :/ not fine with me at all and I agree it should be at least as hard as u say but it's not really... thank u for ur answer anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:02:40-07:00","id":889680,"title":"","content":"&quot;&quot;&quot;We are all the sum of our previous selves, and with this spell a mage can call those afterimages forth. Cast upon an object, area, or living being, this spell replaces its subject with an earlier version of itself, chosen by the caster. Without the Temporal Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to the present, but this is still sufficient to remove most Conditions and heal injuries. By employing Temporal Sympathy, the mage can restore ancient ruins to their inhabited state, return her en-emies to childhood, or even bring the dead back to life. When the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject immediately returns to its present self. Injuries, Conditions, and other effects imposed on the subject while Temporal Summoning is in effect transfer to the present version of the subject when it returns.&quot;&quot;<br /> <br /> Really looks like an error to me no Whitstand no reach for affecting supernaturals.. this doesn't make any sense . I agree with satchel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T00:29:11-07:00","id":889721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889648#post889648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Acanthus trick:<br /> <br /> Lucky Mana Reactor: At chargen, set your Gnosis at 3 by spending all your bonus points on it. Then set your highest Arcanum to Fate 3 and pick Exceptional Luck as a Praxes. Gnosis 3 + Fate 3 = 6 dice, or, on average 3 successes. Since it's a Praxes, you'll be considered rolling an exceptional success on your spell casting roll with three successes. One of the options on a exceptional success is to not only regain all mana spent, but to gain one additional point of mana. Considering it's omni-applicability you'll be casting it a lot, and with that extra Reach you'll be casting it quickly. This means on average you'll be generating more mana than you put in to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On d10's you're not going to average 3 successes on 6 dice. You'd be averaging 3 successes between 9 and 10 dice. Granted, you could be spending willpower on every one of these rolls but then you're just trading Willpower for mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T00:47:19-07:00","id":889729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sufferian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889721#post889721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On d10's you're not going to average 3 successes on 6 dice. You'd be averaging 3 successes between 9 and 10 dice. Granted, you could be spending willpower on every one of these rolls but then you're just trading Willpower for mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I forgot that 10s didn't count as double successes. Really wish they'd stop alternating how basic dice rolls work with every game that uses the ST system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T01:40:21-07:00","id":889745,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sufferian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889721#post889721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On d10's you're not going to average 3 successes on 6 dice. You'd be averaging 3 successes between 9 and 10 dice. Granted, you could be spending willpower on every one of these rolls but then you're just trading Willpower for mana.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889729#post889729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I forgot that 10s didn't count as double successes. Really wish they'd stop alternating how basic dice rolls work with every game that uses the ST system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still; If you are casting it reflexively at that rate, you could always apply your persona Yantra (+1-4) to assure that you have 10 dice to cast - the first yantra is reflexive unless otherwise noted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think I like this trick - not because I feel it's over powered, but because at that point you are quite literally gambling for extra mana. I mean, what could be more in line with the Fate Arcana than that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:20:11-07:00","id":892004,"title":"","content":"hey guys i wanted to know ur opinion on the tilt caused by hexes like arm wreck or leg wreck.. Do these tilts heal or get resolved if the target is able to regenerate damage or should they be dispelled like any other magic? this causes a problem with supernatural beings able to regenerate (basically all of them since vampire have blood werewolves essence and mages can heal with mana) and in the tilt section the tilt explicitly says that to end the tilt if it is caused by damage it can be ended by healing.. so what if the tilt isn't cause by any real damage at all? can i just shrug it off with a blood point or mana or should u use a prime dispell or a fate counterspell?<br /> <br /> i imagine an hex like this can easily be explained not only by &quot;broken&quot; bones and meat but also by paralysis and straight up total dysfunction of ur body like genetic diseases or something like that so not related with regeneration at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 05-16-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:23:25-07:00","id":892007,"title":"","content":"You can, but that's your action. Usually spells that apply tilts do so as a rider effect, meaning you did something bad to them and they wasted an action to fix only half of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:39:36-07:00","id":892024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=892007#post892007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, but that's your action. Usually spells that apply tilts do so as a rider effect, meaning you did something bad to them and they wasted an action to fix only half of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thank u for ur fast answer but i don't fully understand it so like for example if i'm a poor gangrel minding my own business and a mean acanthus use an hex to break both my leg and my arm, do i have to spend two blood points and waste my turn healing or can i just shrug it off reflexively and punch him in the face in the same turn?<br /> also do u happen to have a reference on how exactly this could work cause i couldn't find any exact rule explanation to that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T18:03:46-07:00","id":892159,"title":"","content":"If you're inflicting just Tilts then he might be able to heal both of them in one go, I don't know on that one.<br /> <br /> If for instance you cause the ground to grab a foe and crush his leg (Leg wrack) then even if he heals the Tilt his leg is still stuck in the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:14:33-07:00","id":892901,"title":"","content":"If you're just inflicting tilts via hexes, then RAW the answer is no, they can't just 'heal' them because the resolution condition for both Arm and Leg Wrack specifies that this only works if the tilt is inflicted as the result of an attack.<br /> <br /> This makes a certain amount of sense; when you think about the fictional/mythical curses that hexes represent, they don't tend to be &quot;limb breaks&quot;, but crippling pain in the limb or it going numb and unresponsive. That's how I would present it to a player; there's no physical injury, but it's too painful/numb to get use out of it.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm pretty sure a Werewolf in Gauru specifically recovers from Arm and Leg Wrack tilts every turn, so that effect should still work?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:36:14-07:00","id":892952,"title":"","content":"Here's a Seer trick:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;The Reason The Pentacle Doesn't Stand A Chance&quot;</b><br /> 1. Be Mastigos (not <i>necessary</i>, but it helps)<br /> 2. Join the Seers - join the Panopticon.<br /> 3. Get Seer Status \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Prelacy \u2022\u2022\u2022.<br /> 4. The Crown of Vision gives you a Weak sympathetic connection to anyone you have no connection to.<br /> 5. You now have access to <i>all the Space bullshit</i>.<br /> 6. ???<br /> 7. Profit!<br /> <br /> At the weakest (Space \u2022\u2022), your Glorious Seer Overseer can use Correspondence and Borrow Threads to rearrange Sympathetic Connections between <i>anyone on the planet</i>. Or you can just use Veil Sympathy to carpet bomb some random schmuck's sympathetic links for shiggles.<br /> <br /> It just goes up from there.<br /> <br /> Technically, the <i>only</i> way to block you from attacking someone sympathetically if you've got the Crown of Vision is if it gets suppressed by Veil Sympathy or a similar effect - destroying the link means you have no connection to them, so Crown of Vision gives you a Weak connection to them.<br /> <br /> The <i>only</i> drawback (besides being at the beck and call of a hateful and tyrannical being - since you're a Seer of the Throne, though, that's what we call a <i>perk</i>) is that you can't improve your fake Weak connection (since it only exists for the purposes of determining whether or not you can use the sympathetic range attainment). On the other hand... you can't be targeted through it.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium gets a tweaked version of this (Egregore \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 gives you a <i>Medium</i> connection to every other Mysterium member as long as you are in a Mysterium sanctum), but it doesn't have the same overwhelming advantage of <i>choice</i>, and it allows people to hit back, which the Crown of Vision <i>doesn't</i>.<br /> <br /> The name is only <i>slightly</i> facetious.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Another Seer trick!<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;When I Say Jump, You Say 'How High'&quot;</b><br /> 1. Be a Mastigos (Mastigos master race! But seriously.) Let's say your shadow name is Mentok.<br /> 2. Join the Seers - join the Hegemony.<br /> 3. Pause for the Crown of Obligation (steady Mana gain<i> is</i> lovely), but we have loftier goals.<br /> 4. Grab Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and Seer Status \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> 5. Spend 2xp to grab a Hollow One.<br /> 7. ???<br /> 8. Profit!<br /> <br /> All Mind spells cast on Hollow Ones are Indefinite. For free. They also start with all Mental and Social Attributes and Skills at 0 dots.<br /> <br /> We want to drop a few spells on the Hollow One.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Social Networking</b> (Making) - 5 dots of Allies. Out of nowhere.<br /> 2. <b>Psychic Reprogramming</b> (Patterning) - Give them a Virtue of Obedient to Mentok, and whatever else you damn well please.<br /> 3. <b>Amorality</b> (Unmaking) - Now delete their Vice. They now act in a way <i>entirely</i> consistent with their Virtue.<br /> 4. <b>Augment Mind</b> (Perfecting) - Give them as high a Manipulation as possible. It'll be at <i>least</i> a five unless you push the Potency higher.<br /> 5. <b>Gain Skill</b> (Patterning) - The Hollow One now has Persuasion \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, at least.<br /> 6. <b>Enhance Skill</b> (Perfecting) - Sorry, I misspoke: Persuasion \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u00b9.<br /> <br /> Now we hand them a phone. And tell them to make a few requests.<br /> <br /> This is all stuff you could do to yourself, or to an ally, or whatever. But the Hollow One is a low maintenance (one Mana every few days - you <i>literally</i> get Mana back every time you do something fun), won't betray you (you get to define <i>all of their memories</i>, and there's the bit where they won't willingly act against their impetus to obey you), and is a great patsy (when the NSA comes knocking to find out who asked one of their employees to upload all that porn onto their servers, you have <i>perfect</i> accountability).<br /> <br /> Is it immoral as fuck? I'm not even going to dignify that with a <i>response</i>, straw man who is asking me questions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">1. Technically speaking, if we're going to be doing silly stuff, applying Enhance Skill to a skill rating you got from Gain Skill is kosher. You ain't stacking anything, because only one of those is actually a bonus. If you find this doubtful, drop Enhance Skill and just pump Gain Skill's Potency instead.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:47:14-07:00","id":892957,"title":"","content":"Seers op, pls nerf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:57:47-07:00","id":892961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=892957#post892957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seers op, pls nerf.</div> </div> </div> </div>omg seers so hax. seer master race.<br /> <br /> (The funny part is that I highlighted the two <i>really good</i> Crown Attainments. The Crown of Doctrine does give you <i>a lot</i> of Mana, but doesn't let you fill up your pool any faster; meanwhile, the Crown of Doctrine gives you Mana every time you fulfil your Vice, and turns you into a Social maneuvering machine. And then the Crown of Fury is <i>nice</i>, but kind of lacklustre unless you hella diversified your Arcana portfolio.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:59:24-07:00","id":892962,"title":"","content":"Crown of Vision is the thing that really got me. Their sympathy game is too strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T21:43:06-07:00","id":893022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=892962#post892962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Crown of Vision is the thing that really got me. Their sympathy game is too strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the limits are <i>substantial</i>, don't get me wrong. It's <i>really hard</i> to get spells through a weak connection, and the Crown is phrased in such a way that you can't improve your pseudo-connection without <i>committing</i> and opening up a way for people to hit back. You can cheat to get a stronger connection (Borrow Thread's someone's marriage for a moment), but anyone could do that; just be a garbage man who's willing to go through people's garbage..<br /> <br /> The real diamond (pardon the pun) is the way you blow through stuff like Occultation like it ain't no thang. Judging from how <i>that's</i> worded, it looks like it works on <i>anything</i> that penalizes your information gathering. That's... rather terrifying.<br /> <br /> The Sympathy thing is just a hilarious shortcut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:19:00-07:00","id":893034,"title":"","content":"Hm, I guess I thought it was stronger than it was, or I overestimated how useful a weak connection to everything was.<br /> <br /> Still,, the Seer's magic game is strong, and I can see why they would make a formidable rival for the Pentacle orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T05:35:08-07:00","id":893218,"title":"","content":"Yep I agree with u. I don't know about werewolves though in the regeneration it doesn't really say that when in gauru they heal all tilts every turn. It just says that they heal if the damage is healed, like every other tilt. So the question remains- can a simple hex curse from an acanthus stop a gauru rampage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:03:32-07:00","id":893229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=892952#post892952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a Seer trick:<br /> <br /> <b>&amp;quot;The Reason The Pentacle Doesn't Stand A Chance&amp;quot;</b><br /> 1. Be Mastigos (not <i>necessary</i>, but it helps)<br /> 2. Join the Seers - join the Panopticon.<br /> 3. Get Seer Status \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Prelacy \u2022\u2022\u2022.<br /> 4. The Crown of Vision gives you a Weak sympathetic connection to anyone you have no connection to.<br /> 5. You now have access to <i>all the Space bullshit</i>.<br /> 6. ???<br /> 7. Profit!<br /> <br /> At the weakest (Space \u2022\u2022), your Glorious Seer Overseer can use Correspondence and Borrow Threads to rearrange Sympathetic Connections between <i>anyone on the planet</i>. Or you can just use Veil Sympathy to carpet bomb some random schmuck's sympathetic links for shiggles.<br /> <br /> It just goes up from there.<br /> <br /> Technically, the <i>only</i> way to block you from attacking someone sympathetically if you've got the Crown of Vision is if it gets suppressed by Veil Sympathy or a similar effect - destroying the link means you have no connection to them, so Crown of Vision gives you a Weak connection to them.<br /> <br /> The <i>only</i> drawback (besides being at the beck and call of a hateful and tyrannical being - since you're a Seer of the Throne, though, that's what we call a <i>perk</i>) is that you can't improve your fake Weak connection (since it only exists for the purposes of determining whether or not you can use the sympathetic range attainment). On the other hand... you can't be targeted through it.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium gets a tweaked version of this (Egregore \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 gives you a <i>Medium</i> connection to every other Mysterium member as long as you are in a Mysterium sanctum), but it doesn't have the same overwhelming advantage of <i>choice</i>, and it allows people to hit back, which the Crown of Vision <i>doesn't</i>.<br /> <br /> The name is only <i>slightly</i> facetious.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Another Seer trick!<br /> <br /> <b>&amp;quot;When I Say Jump, You Say 'How High'&amp;quot;</b><br /> 1. Be a Mastigos (Mastigos master race! But seriously.) Let's say your shadow name is Mentok.<br /> 2. Join the Seers - join the Hegemony.<br /> 3. Pause for the Crown of Obligation (steady Mana gain<i> is</i> lovely), but we have loftier goals.<br /> 4. Grab Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and Seer Status \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> 5. Spend 2xp to grab a Hollow One.<br /> 7. ???<br /> 8. Profit!<br /> <br /> All Mind spells cast on Hollow Ones are Indefinite. For free. They also start with all Mental and Social Attributes and Skills at 0 dots.<br /> <br /> We want to drop a few spells on the Hollow One.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Social Networking</b> (Making) - 5 dots of Allies. Out of nowhere.<br /> 2. <b>Psychic Reprogramming</b> (Patterning) - Give them a Virtue of Obedient to Mentok, and whatever else you damn well please.<br /> 3. <b>Amorality</b> (Unmaking) - Now delete their Vice. They now act in a way <i>entirely</i> consistent with their Virtue.<br /> 4. <b>Augment Mind</b> (Perfecting) - Give them as high a Manipulation as possible. It'll be at <i>least</i> a five unless you push the Potency higher.<br /> 5. <b>Gain Skill</b> (Patterning) - The Hollow One now has Persuasion \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, at least.<br /> 6. <b>Enhance Skill</b> (Perfecting) - Sorry, I misspoke: Persuasion \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u00b9.<br /> <br /> Now we hand them a phone. And tell them to make a few requests.<br /> <br /> This is all stuff you could do to yourself, or to an ally, or whatever. But the Hollow One is a low maintenance (one Mana every few days - you <i>literally</i> get Mana back every time you do something fun), won't betray you (you get to define <i>all of their memories</i>, and there's the bit where they won't willingly act against their impetus to obey you), and is a great patsy (when the NSA comes knocking to find out who asked one of their employees to upload all that porn onto their servers, you have <i>perfect</i> accountability).<br /> <br /> Is it immoral as fuck? I'm not even going to dignify that with a <i>response</i>, straw man who is asking me questions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">1. Technically speaking, if we're going to be doing silly stuff, applying Enhance Skill to a skill rating you got from Gain Skill is kosher. You ain't stacking anything, because only one of those is actually a bonus. If you find this doubtful, drop Enhance Skill and just pump Gain Skill's Potency instead.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok finished reading it. And now I wonder how the hell diamond mages managed to survive til.now LOL<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> on another side note--- guys to u think that acanthus get easily infinite spell stacking ? It's not even that hard, u simply continue to cast exceptional luck and add potency to cast even more powerful except luck for x turn and in 1 hour or so u get an exceptional luck roll to cast at 15 potency and 8 reroll and if u want from there u can just use shifting sands to go back the previous scene and start again.. so if I get our of my sanctum after a whole day of this routine I might as well have a monkey paw knife that deal 40 dices extra on an attack ( as bonus equipment) and reroll 8 for 20 dice roll for a week... and this is just the silliest of use if I use 2 reach I can add 20 dices to all.my spellcasting roll for a month or something. Am I wrong? What stops an acanthus from simply accumulating devastating exceptional luck In less than 10 rounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:12:48-07:00","id":893233,"title":"","content":"It's not a Yantra bonus, so technically it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:33:44-07:00","id":893245,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't see anyone who meets the prerequisites <i>not</i> taking Between the Ticks or Fast Spells - hell, they seem to be <i>required</i> for any combat wombat Mage.<br /> <br /> For reference: take a -1 penalty to initiative, get +1 to your action this turn, and aimed spells ignore Defense as if they were a Firearms attack. This takes Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022, Firearms \u2022\u2022, and Time \u2022, which is <i>incredibly trivial</i> and easy to justify for pretty much anyone.<br /> <br /> Not broken, just something that <i>everyone</i> who wants to use combat-time spells is going to go for. <hr /><br /> More hilariously, Occultation, Potent Nimbus and Potent Resonance are not mutually exclusive. This <i>pleases</i> me.<br /> <br /> You have Gnosis 4? No, you have Gnosis 8 for the purposes of your Nimbus' effects, Gnosis 6 for the purposes of flaring, Gnosis 1 for how noticeable it is, and anyone who takes a closer look gets a face full of Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 05-18-2016, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:24:44-07:00","id":893285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889574#post889574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spell can be used without Temporal Sympathy on Unchanged-level past versions of the subject without another listed Withstand rating, which, yeah, seems more like an error than an actual problem with the spell itself given that a higher-level spell capable of a similar feat is Withstood and doesn't have quite the baseline potential to outright reduce the target's Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it is an error, has anyone brought it up in the errata thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:26:46-07:00","id":893286,"title":"","content":"Between the Ticks is bad. It's +1 for -1, once per scene, for 2 xp. FastSpells are cool..burt have issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:36:09-07:00","id":893290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=893286#post893286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the Ticks is bad. It's +1 for -1, once per scene, for 2 xp. FastSpells are cool..burt have issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apparently misread Between the Ticks as not having a once per scene limit. That's what we call &quot;wishful thinking&quot;, because Between the Ticks is really, really <i>bad</i>.<br /> <br /> 2xp is about equal to &quot;+1 die to stuff in a broad circumstance&quot;; with the initiative penalty included it would be totally fine as an at-will thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:15:49-07:00","id":893371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=893285#post893285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If it is an error, has anyone brought it up in the errata thread?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/881992-mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-errata-thread?p=889577#post889577\">Last week</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:07:59-07:00","id":894722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=892962#post892962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Crown of Vision is the thing that really got me. Their sympathy game is too strong.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't it a double edged sword, I meanif you have sympathy to everyone, don't they have it with you too? Doesn't it make it easier for Pentacle Mages to target you too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:16:56-07:00","id":894730,"title":"","content":"Sympathy isn't automatically two way, so the Prelate benefits from Sympathy to everyone but potential targets don't benefit.<br /> <br /> It is entirely possible to develop a strong sympathy to a target and that they won't enjoy a strong sympathy to you. You might love your car for instance, but unless it's sapient it's likely to &quot;feel&quot; pretty indifferent about you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-20-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:29:42-07:00","id":894801,"title":"","content":"But once you use the sympathy they get to use that channel back to you at the same strength. (If they are prepared to react. It is not paranoia if they are after you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:38:22-07:00","id":894808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=894801#post894801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But once you use the sympathy they get to use that channel back to you at the same strength. (If they are prepared to react. It is not paranoia if they are after you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not, as far as I'm aware you are penalized by your Sympathy to return fire down someone else's sympathetic link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T15:20:40-07:00","id":895038,"title":"","content":"Fast Spells is really really handy, barring going up against an Acanthus. (They get defence against firearms, so will avoid it quite easily.) Its main benefit is that you don't need to burn a Reach on making a spell sensory range to have a good shot at hitting people with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T15:51:23-07:00","id":895064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=895038#post895038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fast Spells is really really handy, barring going up against an Acanthus. (They get defence against firearms, so will avoid it quite easily.) Its main benefit is that you don't need to burn a Reach on making a spell sensory range to have a good shot at hitting people with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastigos also get Defence against Firearms. It's actually weird that Life Armor doesn't grant you Defence-Vs-Firearms, as it gives you super-instinct too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:18:11-07:00","id":895098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=895064#post895064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastigos also get Defence against Firearms. It's actually weird that Life Armor doesn't grant you Defence-Vs-Firearms, as it gives you super-instinct too.</div> </div> </div> </div>kind-of, but animals still have a hard time dodging gun fire.<br /> <br /> page 194<br /> Life Armor heightens the combat instincts of the mage and<br /> prepares her body to shrug off injuries.<br /> Life Armor adds half the character\u2019s Life rating (round up) as<br /> both general armor and a bonus to Defense. Use the higher of the<br /> character\u2019s Wits and Dexterity as Defense, rather than the lower.<br /> <br /> They get half their life as bonus defense and armor, so its spilting the difference, and a nice effectent bonus at the odd levels 3 and 5. And a sneaky buff on the dex or wit adding to your def. Most of the time I see it granting a plus1, but its still really nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:25:29-07:00","id":895104,"title":"","content":"Don't forget about Honing the Form. Combine that with Life armour for truly scary defence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:32:37-07:00","id":895113,"title":"","content":"Simply infinite acanthus pun pun- keep casting with rote and penalties each turn exceptional luck to power up another cast of exceptional luck the next turn and then cast it again with more penalties ecc..., each time u can add a -2 at least cumulative to increase the potency of the spell, and also get the steadfast condition or reroll 8 on the spell roll<br /> - So u can cast an exceptional luck with a penalty of -10 and still manage to succeed at casting with a single success (steadfast)- u will easily realize by doing the math that u can cast an exceptional luck spell of +20 dices with reroll 8 for 20 dices roll or something, also u can simply have a +20 in general to use on any action u need. talking about god mode- Also, if time is an issue and u want to keep rolling and accumulating success over success-.... simply rewind and go back to the beginning of the scene with shifting sands. Enjoy infinite bonus dices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:50:21-07:00","id":895247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sufferian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889721#post889721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On d10's you're not going to average 3 successes on 6 dice. You'd be averaging 3 successes between 9 and 10 dice. Granted, you could be spending willpower on every one of these rolls but then you're just trading Willpower for mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>A d10 with 10-again produces on average, exactly 1/3 of a success per die. It takes 9 dice to produce exactly 3 successes on average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T20:13:07-07:00","id":895258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=894730#post894730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy isn't automatically two way</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of sympathetic links is that they <i>are links</i>, i.e. they're discrete phenomena that connect one person/place/thing to another.<br /> <br /> The Crown of Vision attaches qualifiers to the Weak connection it provides that prevent it from being used as a universal conduit back to the Prelate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T12:28:31-07:00","id":895628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=895258#post895258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire point of sympathetic links is that they <i>are links</i>, i.e. they're discrete phenomena that connect one person/place/thing to another.<br /> <br /> The Crown of Vision attaches qualifiers to the Weak connection it provides that prevent it from being used as a universal conduit back to the Prelate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, though my point was that the link is not equally strong in both directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:18:34-07:00","id":896214,"title":"","content":"The Shadow Name merit seems to have amazing potential - sweet sweet +3 tool bonus - until I actually try to think of one.<br /> Any ideas on brokenly applicable Shadow Names, with a very wide range of spells you can apply them to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:34:29-07:00","id":896219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896214#post896214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow Name merit seems to have amazing potential - sweet sweet +3 tool bonus - until I actually try to think of one.<br /> Any ideas on brokenly applicable Shadow Names, with a very wide range of spells you can apply them to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magnus, Merlin, Baba Yaga, Koschei, Gandalf, Circe, Gwydion, Rand Al Thor, Odin... Basically any name broadly associated with magic and wizardry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:07:26-07:00","id":896247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896219#post896219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnus, Merlin, Baba Yaga, Koschei, Gandalf, Circe, Gwydion, Rand Al Thor, Odin... Basically any name broadly associated with magic and wizardry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only imagine the unmitigated chutzpah and lack of originality of a newly awakened apprentice trying to claim a name like Merlin, Odin or Baba Yaga.<br /> <br /> I imagine that very early on in their magical careers, a master or three disabuses these whelps with such delusions of grandeur. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:11:48-07:00","id":896250,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that list. It does bring to mind a concern though.<br /> Does it work on the general symbol of that name being &quot;powerful magic-user in general&quot; and just let you add the +3 to pretty much anything, or would you apply it only to spells that persona would have used?<br /> <br /> For example, Gandalf's cool and all, but he doesn't really cast spells all that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:18:53-07:00","id":896256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896250#post896250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for that list. It does bring to mind a concern though.<br /> Does it work on the general symbol of that name being &quot;powerful magic-user in general&quot; and just let you add the +3 to pretty much anything, or would you apply it only to spells that persona would have used?<br /> <br /> For example, Gandalf's cool and all, but he doesn't really cast spells all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pulling shit like this<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4UfAL9f74I\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4UfAL9f74I\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4UfAL9f74I </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4UfAL9f74I\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4UfAL9f74I </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> gets you the +3 bonus BUT You've tangled yourself in that ID and fate, without the benefit of actually being Gandalf.<br /> <br /> Your party is running from GhostRider, you stop and preform your spell, saving the party; but on his turn, the biker chain pulls you down and away from your party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:22:37-07:00","id":896258,"title":"","content":"I think you're forget the best shadow name<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Usidore, Wizard of the </span></span><a href=\"http://magictavern.wikidot.com/culture-of-foon\" target=\"_blank\">12th Realm of Ephysiyies</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">, Master of Light and Shadow, Manipulator of Magical Delights, Devourer of Chaos, Champion of the </span></span><a href=\"http://magictavern.wikidot.com/great-halls-of-terr-akkas\" target=\"_blank\">Great Halls of Terr'akkas</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">. The elves know me as Fi\u2019ang Yalok. The dwarves know me as Zoenen Hoogstandjes. I am also known in the </span></span><a href=\"http://magictavern.wikidot.com/foon\" target=\"_blank\">Northeast</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> as Gaismun\u0113nas Meistar.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11776-neotoma","name":"Neotoma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:23:12-07:00","id":896260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896250#post896250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it work on the general symbol of that name being &quot;powerful magic-user in general&quot; and just let you add the +3 to pretty much anything, or would you apply it only to spells that persona would have used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematic cohesion remains a concern, even if you discount the inherent complications of choosing a Shadow Name with associated pitfalls and destinies \u2014 most classical wizardly Shadow Names aren't going to help you with spells to hack a database, for example, and taking the name of a villain or well-known antagonist is going to do spooky things to your symbolism regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:24:33-07:00","id":896262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896250#post896250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for that list. It does bring to mind a concern though.<br /> Does it work on the general symbol of that name being &quot;powerful magic-user in general&quot; and just let you add the +3 to pretty much anything, or would you apply it only to spells that persona would have used?<br /> <br /> For example, Gandalf's cool and all, but he doesn't really cast spells all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You need to determine what a name symbolizes, and you may then use those symbols as Yantras. For instance, a mage with a name like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odin\" target=\"_blank\">Odin </a>could employ Norse or Germanic runes or symbols to benefit certain healing, death, royalty, knowledge and battle spells.<br /> <br /> You cannot simply choose a &quot;powerful&quot; or &quot;magical&quot; name such as Merlin or Gandalf and automatically get a +3 bonus to all spells. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadow Name (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect: Your character has a particularly developed magical<br /> persona, and is almost a different person when acting as a mage<br /> than in her mundane life. When purchasing this Merit, determine the<br /> Shadow Name and its symbolism. The character may use those symbols<br /> as a persona tool in spellcasting, worth this Merit\u2019s dots. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:30:17-07:00","id":896267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896247#post896247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can only imagine the unmitigated chutzpah and lack of originality of a newly awakened apprentice trying to claim a name like Merlin, Odin or Baba Yaga.<br /> <br /> I imagine that very early on in their magical careers, a master or three disabuses these whelps with such delusions of grandeur.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, fuck off. The book suggests both Hercules and Odin as valid shadow names. Not everyone needs to be Grhandchandra the Original, Deine or Shesmu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:32:13-07:00","id":896306,"title":"","content":"Titles are good.Bob, THE XYZ is a very nice Shadow Name, because THE XYZ can describe your role and Persona better than &quot;just a Name&quot;. This is why I'm kinda sad the merit is called Shadow Name, not Shadow Persona or something, because &quot;The Necrodetective&quot; is as valid and probably much easier to &quot;get into&quot; Shadow Name as Merlin or Odin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:32:17-07:00","id":896307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896267#post896267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, fuck off. The book suggests both Hercules and Odin as valid shadow names. Not everyone needs to be Grhandchandra the Original, Deine or Shesmu.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Virtually any name is &quot;valid,&quot; but the mage still has to be able to pull it off, no less in order to get the Shadow Name Merit bonus.<br /> <br /> A Gnosis 1 mage, that's at most a first degree disciple, strutting into a consilium meeting and demanding to be addressed as Merlin or Gandalf will quickly be met with snickering and a &quot;sure you are, we had three Merlins just last week.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-22-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:43:51-07:00","id":896314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum