v class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Misterscruffles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896594#post896594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better yet, pick a tarot card. &quot;Death&quot; works great for Moros and Thyrsus, &quot;The World&quot; works for Mastigos and Acanthus, Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going too broad can result in hazardous symbolic blowback \u2014 using balancing qualifiers is invaluable for controlling what your magic might steer towards.<br /> <br /> \u2026I was going to make a joke about Stands here, but now I've just tied that era of JoJo into Tolkein's wizard-colors. Damn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:38:22-07:00","id":896611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896598#post896598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going too broad can result in hazardous symbolic blowback \u2014 using balancing qualifiers is invaluable for controlling what your magic might steer towards.<br /> <br /> \u2026I was going to make a joke about Stands here, but now I've just tied that era of JoJo into Tolkein's wizard-colors. Damn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing worse than symbolic blowback.<br /> <br /> I don't care if you're a master of both Matter and Prime, if that stuff gets on your clothes, it's never coming out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:56:41-07:00","id":896617,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think what's some good unexpected cabal and and shadow names<br /> <br /> Like Pirate themed; Capt, First Mate, Quartermaster, Powder Monkey<br /> Or trickster gods, Coyote/Fox/Spider/Serpent <br /> <br /> Captain Coyote, First among Foxes, Quarters the spider, Ignius Howler<br /> <br /> ok those are horrible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11776-neotoma","name":"Neotoma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:05:38-07:00","id":896622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neotoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896617#post896617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think what's some good unexpected cabal and and shadow names<br /> <br /> Like Pirate themed; Capt, First Mate, Quartermaster, Powder Monkey<br /> Or trickster gods, Coyote/Fox/Spider/Serpent<br /> <br /> Captain Coyote, First among Foxes, Quarters the spider, Ignius Howler<br /> <br /> ok those are horrible</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the Game of Geometric Perfection, i.e., the baseball themed cabal, was deemed acceptable for multiple supplements as well a story in the Mage Fiction Anthology, there's nothing too odd or unexpected for a cabal theme.<br /> <br /> I vote for a cabal theme of Monopoly, and with each Mage in the cabal based off a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monopoly_(game)#Tokens\" target=\"_blank\">Monopoly token.</a><br /> <br /> I wouldn't mess with Battleship and Racecar, but Thimble is a pushover. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T02:06:58-07:00","id":896649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=896622#post896622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the Game of Geometric Perfection, i.e., the baseball themed cabal, was deemed acceptable for multiple supplements as well a story in the Mage Fiction Anthology, there's nothing too odd or unexpected for a cabal theme.<br /> <br /> I vote for a cabal theme of Monopoly, and with each Mage in the cabal based off a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monopoly_(game)#Tokens\" target=\"_blank\">Monopoly token.</a><br /> <br /> I wouldn't mess with Battleship and Racecar, but Thimble is a pushover.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah but thimble is quite the temptress. I hear she caught a changeling's heart and managed to get their whole freehold to treat her as their mother and have them ferry her to and from the hedge.<br /> (Yes I had to make a Peter pan reference)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:11:50-07:00","id":896899,"title":"","content":"The Tower Gang from Kerberos Club seems like it would be neat:<br /> <br /> Big Ben, Big Hand, Little Hand, The Face, and Tick Tock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:05:10-07:00","id":897098,"title":"","content":"Book, movie and song titles. All of them give a common theme while at the same time providing massive diversity.<br /> <br /> On another note, I recall someone calling their Free Councillor &quot;This Machine Kills Fascists&quot;, which is kind of perfect.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're reckless you will run into a certain Guardian. He's gross, he will make your life miserable and no matter what you do, you will never get rid of him for good. No one in the Consilium wants to deal with Herpes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T16:18:32-07:00","id":897308,"title":"","content":"Mana Sensitivity is a underestimated gem. It's great for detecting presence of other mages, even if they try to fool you using some Veiling spells, as there are not many people who will veil *their Mana*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:03:04-07:00","id":897353,"title":"","content":"Jumping the gate a bit there.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hallows and stored Mana trigger her Peripheral Mage Sight, even without an active magical effect.&quot; <br /> <br /> stored mana most likely reference to magical atrifacts, and tass. Which any good mage should keep around. The other way is a little too much insight for a one dot merit. Still very usefull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:05:12-07:00","id":897355,"title":"","content":"Mana is stored in your Pattern. That's probably how Mages can nab newly Awakened so good, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:16:40-07:00","id":897363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=897355#post897355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana is stored in your Pattern. That's probably how Mages can nab newly Awakened so good, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah but techincally everything has mana in their pattern. Thats the reason why blood sacrifcie works. Its not so much stored as it is IN and OF the mage.<br /> <br /> But we can still work with the idea. Give it a two dot upgradeble dot option. The upgraded option will let you see the mana in patterns, even know exactlly much is in it. Much like Supernal Vision","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:42:14-07:00","id":897380,"title":"","content":"Kinda want to give it to WHW on this one; The act of sacrifice itself <i>produces</i> mana rather than releases stored mana - you basically sacrifice a being and receive magical power by converting them into a sacrament. It seems they base the amount you get on the quality of the sacrament <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or, on the quality of the soul if you prefer. <hr /><br /> On a note on the pun-puns. Did the math; It is actually not 'unlimited' per se - you will eventually reach a state where you are at more than -5 and cannot cast the effect; Still - exceptional luck and rote enhance skill are still pretty OP.<br /> <br /> Edit: However, Exceptional Luck + Enhance Skill will result in infinite increases, provided you do add a duration to those effects. Its just using only 1 progressively lowers your casting dice pool by one as you increase potency. But mixing them up doesn't. So... Cool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-23-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:43:48-07:00","id":897382,"title":"","content":"Mana in a Cat is different from a Mana stockpiled by Mage or stockpiled in a Hallow. The best thing that showcases is that you can't manipulate Mana-in-a-Cat using Prime, while Prime magic considers Mage's private pool, Artifact's pool, and Hallow pools to be functionally the same. Example: Channel Mana won't allow you to extract Mana from cats, but works on Hallows, other Mages, Artifacts and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:14:10-07:00","id":897399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=897380#post897380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda want to give it to WHW on this one; The act of sacrifice itself <i>produces</i> mana rather than releases stored mana - you basically sacrifice a being and receive magical power by converting them into a sacrament. It seems they base the amount you get on the quality of the sacrament <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or, on the quality of the soul if you prefer. <hr /><br /> On a note on the pun-puns. Did the math; It is actually not 'unlimited' per se - you will eventually reach a state where you are at more than -5 and cannot cast the effect; Still - exceptional luck and rote enhance skill are still pretty OP.<br /> <br /> Edit: However, Exceptional Luck + Enhance Skill will result in infinite increases, provided you do add a duration to those effects. Its just using only 1 progressively lowers your casting dice pool by one as you increase potency. But mixing them up doesn't. So... Cool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page87mage2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, Blood Sacrifice offers Mana. In an Act of Hubris,<br /> the mage kills a living being for Mana. Its death <b>releases<br /> Mana from its Pattern.</b> A small animal offers one Mana,<br /> while human sacrifices offer as much Mana as the person<br /> had Integrity dots remaining before the killing blow. The<br /> Mana gained from Sacrifice ignores the spend/Turn limits<br /> on Mana if the sacrifice is part of a spell\u2019s casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana is not produced but released from that pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page122mage2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sacrament<br /> A sacrament is any Magical Tool symbolic of the spell in question<br /> that the mage destroys during casting. Many times \u2014 though<br /> by no means always \u2014 it also provides a sympathetic link to the<br /> subject of her spell. She may infuse bread with herbs and spices<br /> to make those who share the loaf work together smoothly. She<br /> may burn a man\u2019s driver\u2019s license and passport for a spell that<br /> removes him from government records. She may fire a male<br /> figure out of clay then crush it to powder when changing her<br /> body to match her gender. If she can find one of her enemy\u2019s<br /> Magical Tools, she has both a sympathetic link and a sacrament<br /> for any spell that would hurt him.<br /> Some mages go further than finding or creating things to sacrifice<br /> during casting. Some engage in quests into the other realms<br /> of the Fallen World, leaving the flesh behind to uncover items<br /> with magical properties of their own. Destroying them during<br /> casting can make a spell flare with power. Particularly twisted<br /> mages kill animals and murder humans for the magical power.<br /> The surest way to kill a powerful enemy with magic is to sacrifice<br /> something close to him \u2014 a beloved pet, or a family member.<br /> Effect: Most sacraments grant a +1 bonus. If the mage has to<br /> spend significant effort to find the right item or component, the<br /> bonus increases to +2, or +3 if the item comes from somewhere<br /> other than the material realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sacrament gives you bonus dice to your spell casting. You can have one item be both though. But mana is not produced, but pulled out of the pattern","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:20:13-07:00","id":897402,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11731_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11731\" data-vbnamecard=\"11731\">MercSet</a> A sacrament in the actual, real world sense my friend. Not the game sense of what it is for a yantra. You don't net mana from just killing something in any way - you net it from specifically sacrificing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: As far as I am aware. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit 2: Though if I'm wrong, and you can stab someone in the middle of combat and kill them and use their mana in that same combat without intentionally meaning to draw forth said mana, by all means I support this endeavor and will hastily exceed my limitations by slaughtering -everyone- in combat at once and using the resulting mana. I don't know what for yet. But it will happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-23-2016, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:32:25-07:00","id":897410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=897382#post897382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana in a Cat is different from a Mana stockpiled by Mage or stockpiled in a Hallow. The best thing that showcases is that you can't manipulate Mana-in-a-Cat using Prime, while Prime magic considers Mage's private pool, Artifact's pool, and Hallow pools to be functionally the same. Example: Channel Mana won't allow you to extract Mana from cats, but works on Hallows, other Mages, Artifacts and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will counter that with<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page86mage2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can keep a certain amount of Mana in their Patterns<br /> depending on their Gnosis dots. Alternatively, tass can be<br /> physically held and carried around in whatever quantities the<br /> mage can stockpile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is a separate pool but it is incorperated into the mage's pattern.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Yes and the game reflects that in its system with a yantra. Yes there are religions and beliefs that have the sacrament as part of its practices. A sacrament yantra is the game term and expresses that idea. The reality of Sacraments in RL space are beyond the scope of this dicussion. Plus I don't want to step on anyone's toes over religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:50:14-07:00","id":897426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=897402#post897402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11731_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11731\" data-vbnamecard=\"11731\">MercSet</a> A sacrament in the actual, real world sense my friend. Not the game sense of what it is for a yantra. You don't net mana from just killing something in any way - you net it from specifically sacrificing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: As far as I am aware. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit 2: Though if I'm wrong, and you can stab someone in the middle of combat and kill them and use their mana in that same combat without intentionally meaning to draw forth said mana, by all means I support this endeavor and will hastily exceed my limitations by slaughtering -everyone- in combat at once and using the resulting mana. I don't know what for yet. But it will happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Channel Mana Withstood by composure. Its a start. It targets, mages, hollows, artifacts, and supernal beings<br /> <br /> But you are correct. the amount of time used to prepare the -harvest- could stand to be clarififed. It would be odd to go from knife death to knife death refilling your mana. As a yantra, it does take a turn to add it to the casting. and channel mana doesn't let you break your mana/turn limit without a reach.<br /> <br /> maybe it takes a number of turns depending on your gnosis(mana/turn limit) to complete the sacrfice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:18:39-07:00","id":897457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=897410#post897410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Yes and the game reflects that in its system with a yantra. Yes there are religions and beliefs that have the sacrament as part of its practices. A sacrament yantra is the game term and expresses that idea. The reality of Sacraments in RL space are beyond the scope of this dicussion. Plus I don't want to step on anyone's toes over religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... The reality of sacraments... is that it's a rite. A thing of religious importance - a sacred act. It does not need to refer to one religion, though is commonly a part of religious practices. I am unsure why it is that using a word for it's actual meaning is 'beyond the scope of this discussion'. But if you prefer -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Self</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You basically sacrifice a being and receive magical power by turning their death into a ritual/ceremony/observance/sacred-act-to-transfer-death-into-mana/process. It seems they base the amount on the quality of the ritual/ceremony/observance/sacred-act-to-transfer-death-into-mana/process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=897426#post897426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Channel Mana Withstood by composure. Its a start. It targets, mages, hollows, artifacts, and supernal beings<br /> <br /> But you are correct. the amount of time used to prepare the -harvest- could stand to be clarififed. It would be odd to go from knife death to knife death refilling your mana. As a yantra, it does take a turn to add it to the casting. and channel mana doesn't let you break your mana/turn limit without a reach.<br /> <br /> maybe it takes a number of turns depending on your gnosis(mana/turn limit) to complete the sacrfice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what the channel mana point is in this. Is that meant for WHW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":"into the list of alternative takes 05-23-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:33:42-07:00","id":897472,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> I meant I can not comment on RL sacraments and their effect in RL. The word is fine. A simple misunderstanding. Mostly I'm shying away from that word, because of Sacrifice's connotation of murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":". 05-23-2016, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:51:53-07:00","id":897495,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11731_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11731\" data-vbnamecard=\"11731\">MercSet</a> Fair enough, I can get behind that. Now that misunderstandings are pushed past, we can get to the subject at hand!<br /> <br /> Seriously though I don't understand the channel mana reference. :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:02:48-07:00","id":897505,"title":"","content":"Channel Mana is a spell that can steal mana from an unwilling target. But you have to deal with it's withstood trait(composure). It was in reference to your thought of killing a guy and taking mana in the same turn. which does give a starting place for mana absorption, and how to model it.<br /> <br /> but I don't know. I mean you could simple make the combat a ritual with the net effect of taking the target's mana. And like I said earlier. the time needed for Blood Sacrifice could stand to be clarififed. Because you could easly go from knife kill to knife kill with full mana. Your wisdom would be s*** but you'd have a full mana pool the whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T21:11:25-07:00","id":897543,"title":"","content":"I could see an Arrow making combat a ritual.<br /> <br /> ... I could see a Praetorian doing the same.<br /> <br /> .... *makes Blood Sacrifice Fighting Style*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T03:03:58-07:00","id":899891,"title":"","content":"It bothers me that you can get infinite willpower and mana. The willpower from when your paradox roll gets a dramatic failure, and mana from getting an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll. The way I see it,you can sit around in your sanctum practicing your praxis, and that somehow restores your mana and willpower over and over and over again. That bothers me because repeatedly casting a praxis is something that's perfectly reasonable from an RP perspective, but quickly leads to complete nonsense from a mechanical perspective. What if the mage has Prime 3? What's stopping him from taking Platonic Form as a praxis, and producing a steady stream of tass water out of nothing?<br /> <br /> I imagine the headlines in all the Consilia: &quot;Apprentice discovers one weird trick Hierarchs don't want you to know about! Break off of the Hallow grid today!&quot;<br /> <br /> Infinite mana tricks annoyed me in Mage 1.0, since it makes no sense that hallows or mana should be valuable if mana is so trivial to produce. I'd like to stamp out infinite mana loops in my Mage 2.0.<br /> <br /> So for possible solutions. Conditions have the whole &quot;one beat per scene&quot; rule to rein them in, but that doesn't quite work here. Resolving a condition takes time, is involved, and most importantly, is interesting. Even if your mage is just handicapping themselves for the purpose of challenging their body, it still produces drama when they're caught in a Seers raid with their pants down.Casting a praxis, on the other hand, is as simple as it gets, and I don't see it producing much drama.<br /> <br /> Say you limit the willpower/mana restoration to once per scene. Even that becomes cheesy. All of a sudden you can't change scenes without giving the players a willpower and mana, and your narrative choices on when to switch scenes now instead become a matter of accounting for all the resources the players are accumulating. &quot;Do I give them a brief scene at the sanctum before we head out? No, that's just yet another opportunity to restore mana and willpower.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-26-2016, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T03:36:32-07:00","id":899899,"title":"","content":"You do realize there's a mana cost in making Tass, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T03:46:05-07:00","id":899904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=899899#post899899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize there's a mana cost in making Tass, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a praxis exeptional success is easier and the cost can be redeemed and you gain an additional mana also","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T04:00:55-07:00","id":899908,"title":"","content":"True, still it's just a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T04:16:58-07:00","id":899913,"title":"","content":"A pretty big chance if you maximize your yantra. Again, Gnosis 3, Prime 3, Willpower 3, and Yantras anywhere from 1 to 5, that's already more Exceptional Successes than normal ones. Channel 2 mana into it as a part of casting; you expended 3 mana, got back 4 from ExSuccess, then ate it to get another 3. Instant Refill.<br /> Just do a social contract with your group and don't roll for narratiely irrelevant spells, especially ones whose sole purpose is to farm. Make it into a cool mystery where Mages try to find out why certain spells can yeld exceptional bonuses (spells cast &quot;mid scene&quot; during &quot;action&quot;) and some won't (off screen farming spells).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-26-2016, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T04:41:15-07:00","id":899920,"title":"","content":"It seems strange to me to even request as a social contract. Then again, I'm used to pretty high pressure games where a moment to get back to the sanctum is a rare event and is frequently spent doing other plot relevant things instead of sitting around trying to game the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T04:55:32-07:00","id":899926,"title":"","content":"This takes you 3 seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:20:55-07:00","id":900351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=899899#post899899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize there's a mana cost in making Tass, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That point of mana is stored in the tass, and can be retrieved with Channel Mana.<br /> <br /> &quot;It has a default Durability of 1 and consists of one point of Mana (which the mage must pay as part of the casting). &quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:26:22-07:00","id":900356,"title":"","content":"Which leads to following:<br /> You create a Tass worth 2 mana. It takes you 2 mana to create it; you can eat it to regain 2 mana. It evens out.<br /> You create a Tass worth 2 mana, generating an Exceptional Success. You pick option to regain all mana used on the spell. It gives you 3 Mana back, and you still can eat your tass to gain 2 mana more.<br /> This can be done as an Instant Action, so you could try it 20 times in a row during a minute, so you have plenty of time to do so when, I don't know, walking around or taking a cab or otherwise between challenges. So a single Obrimos can, if you are doing it as written, solve all Mana problems of your Cabal literally at 0XP by just taking Prime 3 as his starting Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-26-2016, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:04:44-07:00","id":900480,"title":"","content":"A lot of that can be fixed by dialling back on Exceptional Successes for spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Make it so you get one Mana back (to a maximum of the amount spent), and a lot of problems die down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:31:49-07:00","id":900503,"title":"","content":"The cost of the spell is one mana. plus one if it is a common or inferior.<br /> <br /> Mana is then transferred to an item. This mana is not refunded with an exceptional sux . The spell is moving mana that costs one mana.<br /> <br /> This is the same situation as a guy spamming a control light. This is a spamming problem not a spell problem. At six dice: %4.23 of 5sux. %32.03 of 3sux<br /> <br /> So the answer is no. 2 times out of 3 you lose one mana. So for every set of three iterations [lose one, lose one, gain two] you're breaking even, but more likely losing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:56:33-07:00","id":900515,"title":"","content":"You pay the Mana as part of the spell's cost. Exceptional Success gives you spell cost+1 in Mana. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Mana <b>spent</b> on the spell is refunded, and the mage <br /> receives one more point of Mana. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cost:1+ Mana</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has a default Durability of 1 and consists of one point of <br /> Mana <b>(which the mage must pay as part of the casting</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Increase Mana capacity by +1 (the mage may fill this Mana <br /> capacity by<b> spending Mana as part of the casting</b> or leave <br /> the tass partially empty) </div> </div> </div>There is no hidden rule or clever wording that stops trick the Strill (other than GM intervention, obviously) pointed out from working. Platonic Form lacks a safety measure in it's wording. It's a good thing to home rule in, because as pointed out, it breaks the Mana economy in half, more than any other recharge trick.<br /> Assuming six dice on a roll is little...unrealistic. Anyone aiming for reliable Exceptional Success on a Praxis is going to Willpower (because, surprise,you regain Willpower when you Exceptionally Succeed on a Spell) and put at least 2 yantras into it. A starting character is going to, with minimal effort, roll 1 (gnosis) + 3 (Prime) + 3 (Willpower) + 2 (High Speech) + 2 (your favorite +2 yantra, can easily be +3 if you pick Shadow Name merit, +4 if you have Cabal Theme or resonant Mana, and +5 if you have both Theme and Resonant mana). That's 11 dice. Which is 66% of exceptional success - which means you not only not lose mana, but get double the investment plus one back, and 98% of one success, which means you lose 1 willpower point and no mana (because you can just eat the tass and reabsorb it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:03:25-07:00","id":900516,"title":"","content":"EDIT: nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:12:16-07:00","id":900519,"title":"","content":"You can't stack yantra like that. You only get two to start at CC and incorporation of each addition one beyond the first takes another action<br /> <br /> mage 2e page 112<br /> Yantras<br /> Yantras are a form of magical shorthand which a mage uses to<br /> help her focus on casting a spell. She can use nearly anything \u2014 an<br /> object, a place, a type of environment, or even a specific set of<br /> actions \u2014 to focus her will and recall her Imago. Using such tools<br /> grants a bonus to the spellcasting dice pool, up to +5 after penalties<br /> depending on the specific Yantra and how many she uses while<br /> casting her spell. See p. 119 for more information on Yantras.<br /> <br /> page 86<br /> Upon Awakening, a mage can only use two Yantras in a<br /> given spellcasting. At higher Gnosis levels, she becomes<br /> able to integrate more Yantras into her casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:15:16-07:00","id":900521,"title":"","content":"...So? You take 6 seconds instead of 3 each time. There is literally no reason to not use your Yantras for spell like this where you are not time pressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:30:57-07:00","id":900528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=900521#post900521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...So? You take 6 seconds instead of 3 each time. There is literally no reason to not use your Yantras for spell like this where you are not time pressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means You have to put take penalties to the casting to keep the item around. gnosis 1 prime 3 willpower 3 yantramax 5(assmuing you have everything perfect) = 12 dice. Now how long do need this tass to be around? I'm going to say it takes an action to destory. so one extra turn (-2) = 10 dice. so yes %66.27 In a controlled white room, you have roughly greater than a coin flip to gain one mana.<br /> <br /> But really the gain is so not worth the extra risk. You never actually gain willpower. Actually you lose willpower on a fail and don't get it back.<br /> [lose one mana :: lose one willpower, gain one mana, gain one mana]<br /> <br /> So again. its not a problem with the spell but a problem of spamming. You can do this exact same thing with any spell. except without the mana cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:41:14-07:00","id":900538,"title":"","content":"You have a Coin Flip+ to gain Mana, and practically no risk of losing Mana. <br /> Exceptional Success refunds you mana that you put into the Tass, gives you one extra, and Tass still has this mana. You not only regained all mana you used up, you also created one mana extra that you could give to other people, for example. I think it's pretty clear why creating Mana out of thin air on pretty consistent basis is bad for economy? You can do stuff like have an Artifact or some other Mana battery, use Platonic Form to create Tass, get your Mana refunded by ExSuccess, and then move Mana from your Tass to your Mana Battery, then let your Platonic Form crumble. Direct consequence: if your party has an Obrimos, they have no need for any kind of Mana regeneration, because they can refill it at any time by pestering Obrimos to do the Platonic Refill. Hell, you could just sell it to other Mages. <br /> <br /> And yes, you do restore Willpower. Exceptional Successes on spells always restore 1 point of Willpower, no matter which option from the menu you pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:31:58-07:00","id":900576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=900538#post900538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, you do restore Willpower. Exceptional Successes on spells always restore 1 point of Willpower, no matter which option from the menu you pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you get another point of willpower if your paradox roll got a dramatic failure, which is a 90% chance of happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-26-2016, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:41:54-07:00","id":900584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=900576#post900576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you get another point of willpower if your paradox roll got a dramatic failure, which is a 90% chance of happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>10%.<br /> <br /> Chance Dice only dramatically fail on a 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T20:07:23-07:00","id":900609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=900538#post900538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, you do restore Willpower. Exceptional Successes on spells always restore 1 point of Willpower, no matter which option from the menu you pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>if you keep having to use willpower, to get the dice pool you want. then you don't gain any willpower. you just get refunded the willpower you just spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T10:56:39-07:00","id":1535854,"title":"","content":"Thread necromancy but this is in topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> What is better from a mechanical point of view, that the Immediate Nimbus grants bonuses or impose penalties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T11:28:18-07:00","id":1535857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=1535854#post1535854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thread necromancy but this is in topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> What is better from a mechanical point of view, that the Immediate Nimbus grants bonuses or impose penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Nimbus can be withstood and with not too much difficulty, I would say the bonus is more reliable than the penalty, because those benefitting from it wouldn't want to resist. The exception would be a combination of <i>Imposing Nimbus</i> with other merits, which could allow for consistently imposing a Persistent Condition (such as Amnesia and Delusional), which adds some interesting utility to the cabal's problemsolving toolkit (like those two conditions creating a neuralizer or Rashomon effect for Guardian characters to cover things up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T11:42:09-07:00","id":1535858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=1535857#post1535857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the Nimbus can be withstood and with not too much difficulty, I would say the bonus is more reliable than the penalty, because those benefitting from it wouldn't want to resist. The exception would be a combination of <i>Imposing Nimbus</i> with other merits, which could allow for consistently imposing a Persistent Condition (such as Amnesia and Delusional), which adds some interesting utility to the cabal's problemsolving toolkit (like those two conditions creating a neuralizer or Rashomon effect for Guardian characters to cover things up).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> Do you get the effects (positive or negative) of your own Immediate Nimbus?<br /> <br /> Can you exclude someone from your Immediate Nimbus? (I wouldnt want to positively affect an enemy for example).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T12:07:35-07:00","id":1535864,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if the caster is affected, I can't find a clarification either confirming or denying it. I would imagine they aren't, since its the way the mage is passively warping reality in their signature manner.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can exclude people by default. When all mages have the Active Sight, they are possibly subjected to any other participant's Nimbus. I imagine a spell could be made with a combination of Fate 2 (<i>Warding Gesture</i>) and Prime 1 (an Unveiling of the Nimbus) to selectively exclude anyone its cast on, or perhaps <i>Warding Gesture</i> by itself could be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T03:38:00-07:00","id":1535980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889072#post889072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pun-Pun like Mastigos trick:<br /> Klara the Mastigos likes Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill, and Enhance Attribute. She likes them so much that she picks them as her Rotes, which key off her favorite Skill.<br /> Klara casts Enhance Skill using her Rote, targeting her Favorite Skill. She pays Mana and Reach to push it over Human limits. Her Favorite Skill is higher, so her Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill and Enhance Attribute dicepools are now bigger. Which means that she can cast Enhance Skill again, with more Potency! This means that her Skill will become bigger, by a point or two than in previous casting, allowing her to repeat this until she arrives at Infinity.<br /> After gaining Infinite Skill, Klara decides to become Infinitely Smart. She casts Enhance Attribute, using her Infinite Dicepool to set her Traits at Infinity. After becoming Infinitely Smart, she understands now what should be done to humanity.<br /> She casts Psychic Domination, with Duration set to Indefinite, and pays Reach to get most powerful command ever imagined. She puts Infinite Factors into everything, so whole Universe is covered by her spell, which has only one command:<br /> WATCH. CAT. VIDEOS.<br /> And then, Klara the Mastigos ascends, becoming Dark Mittens Mittens, Exarch of Control Through Kittens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love the character. But my ocd demands me to tell you that all bonuses or minuses are of max +5. Rote yantra therefore this cant be abused like that ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T12:48:41-07:00","id":1544351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=889072#post889072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pun-Pun like Mastigos trick:<br /> Klara the Mastigos likes Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill, and Enhance Attribute. She likes them so much that she picks them as her Rotes, which key off her favorite Skill.<br /> Klara casts Enhance Skill using her Rote, targeting her Favorite Skill. She pays Mana and Reach to push it over Human limits. Her Favorite Skill is higher, so her Psychic Domination, Enhance Skill and Enhance Attribute dicepools are now bigger. Which means that she can cast Enhance Skill again, with more Potency! This means that her Skill will become bigger, by a point or two than in previous casting, allowing her to repeat this until she arrives at Infinity.<br /> After gaining Infinite Skill, Klara decides to become Infinitely Smart. She casts Enhance Attribute, using her Infinite Dicepool to set her Traits at Infinity. After becoming Infinitely Smart, she understands now what should be done to humanity.<br /> She casts Psychic Domination, with Duration set to Indefinite, and pays Reach to get most powerful command ever imagined. She puts Infinite Factors into everything, so whole Universe is covered by her spell, which has only one command:<br /> WATCH. CAT. VIDEOS.<br /> And then, Klara the Mastigos ascends, becoming Dark Mittens Mittens, Exarch of Control Through Kittens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mudras can only add up to +6 even if your skill is higher","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28510-communist-owl","name":"Communist Owl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28510_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T19:58:30-07:00","id":1549331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Communist Owl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889004-the-broken-topic-power-hungry-players-let-s-discuss-necro?p=1544351#post1544351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mudras can only add up to +6 even if your skill is higher</div> </div> </div> </div>There is some question about getting to +7.<br /> <br /> Or whether it is called at +5 regardless of Order rote speciality - pretty sure this was the intended plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> For +7 you require membership of the historic order Keepers of the Word, and the Exoteric Arete order merit, which requires you to choose a single skill, and then gives +3 on non-magical rolls, but also treats the skill as if it were an order rote skill of it isn't and gives and extra dice if it already is an order rote skill... So Academics, Expression or Occult...<br /> <br /> So by the previous argument, this would still be limited to +5, but since this was written after and the merit requires a skill with 4 dots or more (+ speciality), it seems the intention is clear to allow 4+2 = 6 for order rote skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added a caveat 03-14-2025, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}